3. Keeping votre tête and your poitrine up, move the resisted leg back as far as you can while keeping the genou straight.
4. Return the leg to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hip_Extension_with_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hip Flexion with Band', 'Quadriceps', 'Élastique', '1. Secure one end of the band to the lower portion of a post and attach the other to one cheville.
2. Face away from the attachment point of the band.
3. Keeping votre tête and your poitrine up, raise your genou up to 90 degrees and pause.
4. Return the leg to the position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hip_Flexion_with_Band/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hip Lift with Band', 'Fessiers', 'Élastique', '1. After choosing a suitable band, lay down in the middle of the rack, after securing the band on either side of you. If your rack doesn''t have pegs, the band can be secured using heavy haltères or similar objects, just ensure they won''t move.
2. Adjust your position so that the band is directly over your hanches. Bend your genous and place vos pieds flat on le sol. vos mains can be on le sol or holding the band in position.
3. Keeping your épaules on the ground, drive through your heels to raise your hanches, pushing into the band as high as you can.
4. Pause at the top of the motion, and Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hip_Lift_with_Band/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hug A Ball', 'Bas du dos', 'Swiss ball', '1. Seat yourself on le sol.
2. Straddle an exercise ball between both legs and lower your hanches down toward le sol.
3. Hug vos bras around the ball to support votre corps. Adjust vos jambes so that vos pieds are flat on le sol and your genous line up over your chevilles. Keep a good grip on the ball so it doesn''t roll away from you and send you back onto your buttocks.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hug_A_Ball/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hug Knees To Chest', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol and pull both genous up to your poitrine.
2. Hold vos bras under the genous, not over (that would put to much pressure on your genou joints).
3. Lentement, pull the genous toward your épaules. This also stretches your buttocks muscles.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hug_Knees_To_Chest/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hurdle Hops', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Set up a row of hurdles or other small barriers, placing them a few feet apart.
2. Stand in front of the first hurdle with vos pieds épaule width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by jumping with both feet over the first hurdle, swinging both arms as you jump.
4. Absorb the impact of landing by bending the genous, rebounding out of the first leap by jumping over the next hurdle. Continue until you have jumped over all of the hurdles.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hurdle_Hops/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hyperextensions (Back Extensions)', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Lie face down on a hyperextension banc, tucking your chevilles securely under the footpads.
2. Adjust the upper pad if possible so your upper cuisses lie flat across the wide pad, leaving enough room for you to bend at the waist without any restriction.
3. With votre corps straight, cross vos bras in front of you (my preference) or behind votre tête. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : You can also hold a poids plate for extra resistance in front of you under your crossed arms.
4. Start bending forward Lentement, at the waist as far as you can while keeping votre dos flat. Inspirez as you perform this movement. Keep moving forward until you feel a nice stretch on the ischio-jambiers and you can no longer keep going without a rounding of the back. Conseil : Never round the back as you perform cet exercice. Also, some people can go farther than others. The key thing is that you go as far as votre corps allows you to without rounding the back.
5. Lentement, raise your torse back to the initial position as you inspirez. Conseil : Avoid the temptation to arch votre dos past a straight line. Also, do not swing the torse at any time in order to protect the back from injury.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hyperextensions_Back_Extensions/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hyperextensions With No Hyperextension Bench', 'Bas du dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. With someone holding down vos jambes, slide yourself down to the edge a flat banc until your hanches hang off the end of the banc. Conseil : Your entire upper body should be hanging down towards le sol. Also, you will be in the same position as if you were on a hyperextension banc but the range of motion will be shorter due to the height of the flat banc vs. that of the hyperextension banc.
2. With votre corps straight, cross vos bras in front of you (my preference) or behind votre tête. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : You can also hold a poids plate for extra resistance in front of you under your crossed arms.
3. Start bending forward Lentement, at the waist as far as you can while keeping votre dos flat. Inspirez as you perform this movement. Keep moving forward until you almost touch le sol or you feel a nice stretch on the ischio-jambiers (whichever comes first). Conseil : Never round the back as you perform cet exercice.
4. Lentement, raise your torse back to the initial position as you expirez. Conseil : Avoid the temptation to arch votre dos past a straight line. Also, do not swing the torse at any time in order to protect the back from injury.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hyperextensions_With_No_Hyperextension_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('IT Band and Glute Stretch', 'Abducteurs', 'Autre', '1. Loop a belt, rope, or band around one of vos pieds, and swing that leg across votre corps to the opposite side, keeping the leg extended as you lay on the ground. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping your foot off of le sol, pull on the belt, using the tension to pull the toes up. Maintenez 10-20 secondes, and Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/IT_Band_and_Glute_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Iliotibial Tract-SMR', 'Abducteurs', 'Foam roller', '1. Lay on your side, with the bottom leg placed onto a foam roller between the hanche and the genou. The other leg can be crossed in front of you.
2. Place as much of your poids as is tolerable onto your bottom leg; there is no need to keep your bottom leg in contact with the ground. Be sure to relax the muscles of the leg you are stretching.
3. Roll your leg over the foam from you hanche to your genou, pausing for 10-30 seconds at points of tension. Répétez with the opposite leg.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Iliotibial_Tract-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Inchworm', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds close together. Keeping vos jambes straight, stretch down and put vos mains on le sol directly in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by walking vos mains forward slowly, alternating your left and your right. As you do so, bend only at the hanche, keeping vos jambes straight.
3. Keep going until votre corps is parallel to the ground in a pushup position.
4. Now, keep vos mains in place and Lentement, take short steps with vos pieds, moving only a few inches at a time.
5. Continue walking until vos pieds are by hour hands, keeping vos jambes straight as you do so.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Inchworm/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Barbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with an prise en pronation (palms down) that is a little closer together than épaule width.
2. Allongez-vous au sol on an incline banc set at any angle between 45-75-degrees.
3. Bring the bar overhead with vos bras extended and coudes in. The arms should be in line with the torse above the head. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Now lower the bar in a semicircular motion behind votre tête until your forearms touch your biceps. Inspirez as you perform this movement. Conseil : Keep your upper arms stationary and close to votre tête en permanence. Only the forearms should move.
5. Revenez en position de départ as you Expirez and you contract the triceps. Hold the contraction for a second.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Barbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Bench Pull', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Grab a haltère in each hand and lie face down on an incline banc that is set to an incline that is approximately 30 degrees.
2. Let the arms hang to your sides fully extended as they point to le sol.
3. Turn the poignets until vos mains have a pronated (palms down) grip.
4. Now flare the coudes out. C''est votre position de départ.
5. As you Expirez, start to pull the haltères up as if you are doing a reverse banc press. You will do this by bending at the coudes and bringing the upper arms up as you let the forearms hang. Continue this motion until the upper arms are at the same level as votre dos. Conseil : The coudes will come out to the side and your upper arms and torse should make the letter "T" at the top of le mouvement. Hold the contraction at the top for a second.
6. Lentement, go back down to the position de départ as you Inspirez.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Bench_Pull/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Cable Chest Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. Adjust the poids to an appropriate amount and be seated, grasping the handles. Your upper arms should be about 45 degrees to the body, with votre tête and poitrine up. The coudes should be bent to about 90 degrees. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by extending through the coude, pressing the handles together straight in front of you. Keep your omoplates retracted as you execute le mouvement.
3. After pausing at full extension, Revenez en position de départ, keeping tension on the cables.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Cable_Chest_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Cable Flye', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. To get yourself into the position de départ, set the pulleys at le sol level (lowest level possible on the machine that is below your torse).
2. Place an incline banc (set at 45 degrees) in between the pulleys, select a poids on each one and grab a pulley on each hand.
3. With a handle on each hand, Allongez-vous sur un banc incliné and bring vos mains together bras tendus in front of your face. C''est votre position de départ.
4. With a slight bend of your coudes (in order to prevent stress at the biceps tendon), lower vos bras out at both sides in a wide arc until you feel a stretch on your poitrine. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Keep in mind that throughout le mouvement, the arms should remain stationary. le mouvement should only occur at the épaule joint.
5. Return vos bras back to the position de départ as you squeeze your poitrine muscles and expirez. Maintenez la position 1 seconde. Conseil : Make sure to use the same arc of motion used to lower the poids.
6. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Cable_Flye/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Dumbbell Bench With Palms Facing In', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on an incline banc with a haltère on each hand on top of your cuisses. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.
2. By using your cuisses to help you get the haltères up, clean the haltères one arm at a time so that you can hold them at épaule width.
3. Once at épaule width, keep the palms of vos mains with a neutral grip (paumes vers each other). Keep your coudes flared out with the upper arms in line with the épaules (perpendiculaire à the torse) and the coudes bent creating a angle de 90 degrés between the upper arm and the forearm. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Now bring down the poids Lentement, to your side as you Inspirez. Keep full control of the haltères en permanence.
5. As you Expirez, push the haltères up using your pectoral muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down slowly. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
6. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
7. When you are done, place the haltères back in your cuisses and then on le sol. This is the safest manner to dispose of the haltères.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Bench_With_Palms_Facing_In/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Dumbbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit back on an incline banc with a haltère in each hand held bras tendus. Keep your coudes close to your torse and rotate the palms of vos mains until they are facing forward. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde.
3. Lentement, begin to bring the haltères back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Dumbbell Flyes', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Hold a haltère on each hand and lie on an incline banc that is set to an incline angle of no more than 30 degrees.
2. Extend vos bras above you with a slight bend at the coudes.
3. Now rotate the poignets so that the palms of vos mains are facing you. Conseil : The pinky fingers should be next to each other. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Inspirez, start to Lentement, lower the arms to the side while keeping the arms extended and while rotating the poignets until the palms of the hand are facing each other. Conseil : At the end of le mouvement the arms will be by your side with the paumes vers the ceiling.
5. As you expirez start to bring the haltères back up to the position de départ by reversing the motion and rotating the hands so that the pinky fingers are next to each other again. Conseil : Keep in mind that le mouvement will only happen at the épaule joint and at the poignet. There is no motion that happens at the coude joint.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Flyes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Dumbbell Flyes - With A Twist', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Hold a haltère in each hand and lie on an incline banc that is set to an incline angle of no more than 30 degrees.
2. Extend vos bras above you with a slight bend at the coudes.
3. Now rotate the poignets so that the palms of vos mains are facing you. Conseil : The pinky fingers should be next to each other. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Inspirez, start to Lentement, lower the arms to the side while keeping the arms extended and while rotating the poignets until the palms of the hand are facing each other. Conseil : At the end of le mouvement the arms will be by your side with the paumes vers the ceiling.
5. As you expirez start to bring the haltères back up to the position de départ by reversing the motion and rotating the hands so that the pinky fingers are next to each other again. Conseil : Keep in mind that le mouvement will only happen at the épaule joint and at the poignet. There is no motion that happens at the coude joint.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Flyes_-_With_A_Twist/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Dumbbell Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on an incline banc with a haltère in each hand atop your cuisses. The palms of vos mains will be facing each other.
2. Then, using your cuisses to help push the haltères up, lift the haltères one at a time so that you can hold them at épaule width.
3. Once you have the haltères raised to épaule width, rotate your poignets forward so that the palms of vos mains are facing away from you. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Be sure to keep full control of the haltères en permanence. Then Expirez and push the haltères up with your poitrine.
5. Lock vos bras at the top, Maintenez la position 1 seconde, and then start Lentement, lowering the poids. Tip Ideally, lowering the poids should take about twice as long as raising them.
6. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
7. When you are done, place the haltères back on your cuisses and then on le sol. This is the safest manner to release the haltères.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Hammer Curls', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Seat yourself on an incline banc with a haltère in each hand. You should pressed firmly against he back with vos pieds together. Allow the haltères to hang straight down at your side, holding them with a neutral grip. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Initiate le mouvement by flexing at the coude, attempting to keep the upper arm stationary.
3. Continue to the top of le mouvement and pause, then Lentement, return to the start position.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Hammer_Curls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Inner Biceps Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Hold a haltère in each hand and Allongez-vous au sol on an incline banc.
2. The haltères should be at arm''s length hanging at your sides and your palms should be facing out. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now as you expirez curl the poids outward and up while keeping your forearms in line with your side deltoids. Continue the curl until the haltères are at épaule height and to the sides of your deltoids. Conseil : The end of le mouvement should look similar to a double biceps pose.
4. After a second contraction at the top of le mouvement, start to inspirez and Lentement, lower the poids back to the position de départ using the same path used to bring them up.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Inner_Biceps_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Push-Up', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand facing banc or sturdy elevated platform. Place hands on edge of banc or platform, slightly wider than épaule width.
2. Position forefoot back from banc or platform with arms and body straight. Arms should be perpendiculaire à body. Keeping body straight, lower poitrine to edge of box or platform by bending arms.
3. Push body up until arms are extended. Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Push-Up Close-Grip', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand facing a Smith machine bar or sturdy elevated platform at an appropriate height.
2. Place vos mains next to one another on the bar.
3. Position vos pieds back from the bar with arms and body straight. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Keeping votre corps straight, lower your poitrine to the bar by bending the arms.
5. Revenez en position de départ by extending the coudes, pressing yourself back up.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Close-Grip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Push-Up Depth Jump', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. For this drill you will need a box about 12 inches high, and two thick mats or aerobics steps.
2. Place the steps just outside of your épaules, and place vos pieds on top of the box so that you are in an incline pushup position, vos mains just inside the steps. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by bending at the coudes to lower votre corps, quickly reversing position to push votre corps off of the ground. As you leave the ground, move vos mains onto the steps, bending your coudes to absorb the impact.
4. Répétez the motion to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Depth_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Push-Up Medium', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand facing a Smith machine bar or sturdy elevated platform at an appropriate height.
2. Place vos mains on the bar, with vos mains about épaule width apart.
3. Position vos pieds back from the bar with arms and body straight. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Keeping votre corps straight, lower your poitrine to the bar by bending the arms.
5. Revenez en position de départ by extending the coudes, pressing yourself back up.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Medium/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Push-Up Reverse Grip', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand facing a Smith machine bar or sturdy elevated platform at an appropriate height.
2. Place vos mains on the bar palms up, with vos mains about épaule width apart.
3. Position vos pieds back from the bar with arms and body straight. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Keeping votre corps straight, lower your poitrine to the bar by bending the arms.
5. Revenez en position de départ by extending the coudes, pressing yourself back up.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Reverse_Grip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Incline Push-Up Wide', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand facing a Smith machine bar or sturdy elevated platform at an appropriate height.
2. Place vos mains on the bar, with vos mains wider than épaule width.
3. Position vos pieds back from the bar with arms and body straight. vos bras should be perpendiculaire à the body. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Keeping votre corps straight, lower your poitrine to the bar by bending the arms.
5. Revenez en position de départ by extending the coudes, pressing yourself back up.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Wide/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Intermediate Groin Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with vos jambes extended. Loop a belt, rope, or band around one of vos pieds, and swing that leg as far to the side as you can. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Pull gently on the belt to create tension in your groin and ischio-jambiers muscles. Maintenez 10-20 secondes, and Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Intermediate_Groin_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Intermediate Hip Flexor and Quad Stretch', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Lie face down on le sol, with a rope, belt, or band looped around one foot.
2. Flex the genou and extend the hanche of the leg to be stretched, using both hands to pull on the belt. Your genou and your hanche should come off of le sol, creating tension in the hanche flexors and quadriceps. Hold the stretch for 10-20 seconds, and Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Intermediate_Hip_Flexor_and_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Internal Rotation with Band', 'Épaules', 'Élastique', '1. Choke the band around a post. The band should be at the same height as your coude. Tenez-vous debout avec your right side to the band a couple of feet away.
2. Grasp the end of the band with your right hand, and keep your coude pressed firmly to your side. We recommend you hold a pad or foam roll in place with your coude to keep it firmly in position.
3. With your upper arm in position, your coude should be flexed to 90 degrees with your hand reaching away from your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Execute le mouvement by rotating your arm in a forehand motion, keeping your coude in place.
5. Continue as far as you are able, pause, and then Revenez en position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Internal_Rotation_with_Band/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Inverted Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Position a bar in a rack to about waist height. You can also use a smith machine.
2. Take a wider than épaule width grip on the bar and position yourself hanging underneath the bar. votre corps should be straight with your heels on the ground with vos bras fully extended. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by flexing the coude, pulling your poitrine towards the bar. Retract your omoplates as you perform le mouvement.
4. Pause at the top of the motion, and return yourself to the start position.
5. Répétez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Inverted_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Inverted Row with Straps', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Hang a rope or suspension straps from a rack or other stable object. Grasp the ends and position yourself in a supine position hanging from the ropes. votre corps should be straight with your heels on the ground with vos bras fully extended. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by flexing the coude, pulling your poitrine to vos mains. Retract your omoplates as you perform le mouvement.
3. Pause at the top of the motion, and return yourself to the start position.
4. Répétez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Inverted_Row_with_Straps/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Iron Cross', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Iron_Cross/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Iron Crosses (stretch)', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Lie face down on le sol, with vos bras extended out to your side, palms pressed to le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
2. To begin, flex one genou and bring that leg across the back of votre corps, attempting to touch it to the ground near the opposite hand.
3. Promptly return the leg to the starting postion, and quickly Répétez with the other leg. Continue alternating for 10-20 repetitions.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Iron_Crosses_stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Isometric Chest Squeezes', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. While either seating or standing, bend vos bras at a angle de 90 degrés and place the palms of vos mains together in front of your poitrine. Conseil : vos mains should be open with the palms together and fingers facing forward (perpendiculaire à your torse).
2. Push both hands against each other as you contract your poitrine. Start with slow tension and increase slowly. Keep breathing normally as you execute this contraction.
3. Hold for the recommended number of seconds.
4. Now release the tension slowly.
5. Rest for the recommended amount of time and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Isometric_Chest_Squeezes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Isometric Neck Exercise - Front And Back', 'Cou', 'Poids de corps', '1. With votre tête and neck in a neutral position (normal position with head erect facing forward), place both of vos mains on the front side of votre tête.
2. Now gently push forward as you contract the neck muscles but resisting any movement of votre tête. Start with slow tension and increase slowly. Keep breathing normally as you execute this contraction.
3. Hold for the recommended number of seconds.
4. Now release the tension slowly.
5. Rest for the recommended amount of time and Répétez with vos mains placed on the back side of votre tête.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Isometric_Neck_Exercise_-_Front_And_Back/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Isometric Neck Exercise - Sides', 'Cou', 'Poids de corps', '1. With votre tête and neck in a neutral position (normal position with head erect facing forward), place your left hand on the left side of votre tête.
2. Now gently push towards the left as you contract the left neck muscles but resisting any movement of votre tête. Start with slow tension and increase slowly. Keep breathing normally as you execute this contraction.
3. Hold for the recommended number of seconds.
4. Now release the tension slowly.
5. Rest for the recommended amount of time and Répétez with your right hand placed on the right side of votre tête.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Isometric_Neck_Exercise_-_Sides/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Isometric Wipers', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Assume a push-up position, supporting your poids on vos mains and toes while keeping votre corps straight. vos mains should be just outside of épaule width. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by shifting votre corps poids as far to one side as possible, allowing the coude on that side to flex as you lower votre corps.
3. Reverse the motion by extending the flexed arm, pushing yourself up and then dropping to the other side.
4. Répétez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Isometric_Wipers/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('JM Press', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Start the exercise the same way you would a close grip banc press. You will Allongez-vous sur un banc plat while holding a barre bras tendus (fully extended) with the coudes in. However, instead of having the arms perpendiculaire à the torse, make sure the bar is set in a direct line above the upper poitrine. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Now beginning from a fully extended position lower the bar down as if performing a lying triceps extension. Inspirez as you perform this movement. When you reach the half way point, let the bar roll back about one inch by moving the upper arms towards vos jambes until they are perpendiculaire à the torse. Conseil : Keep the bend at the coudes constant as you bring the upper arms forward.
3. As you expirez, press the bar back up by using the triceps to perform a close grip banc press.
4. Now go back to the position de départ and start over.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/JM_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Jackknife Sit-Up', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol (or exercise mat) on votre dos with vos bras extended straight back behind votre tête and vos jambes extended also. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you expirez, bend at the waist while simultaneously raising vos jambes and arms to meet in a jackknife position. Conseil : The legs should be extended and lifted at approximately a 35-angle de 45 degrés from le sol and the arms should be extended and parallel to vos jambes. The upper torse should be off le sol.
3. While inhaling, lower vos bras and legs back to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Jackknife_Sit-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Janda Sit-Up', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Position votre corps on le sol in the basic sit-up position; genous to a ninety degree angle with feet flat on le sol and arms either crossed over your poitrine or to the sides. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you strongly tighten your fessiers and ischio-jambiers, fill your lungs with air and in a slow (three to six second count) ascent, Lentement, expirez. Conseil : It is important to tighten the fessiers and ischio-jambiers as this will cause the hanche flexors to be inactivated in a process called reciprocal inhibition, which basically means that opposite muscles to the contracted ones will relax.
3. As you inspirez, Lentement, go back in a controlled manner to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Janda_Sit-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Jefferson Squats', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Place a barre on le sol.
2. Stand in the middle of the bar length wise.
3. Bend down by bending at the genous and keeping votre dos straight and grasp the front of the bar with your right hand. Your palm should be in (neutral grip) facing the left side.
4. Grasp the rear of the bar with your left hand. The palm of your hand should be in neutral grip alignment (paumes vers the right side). Conseil : Ensure that your grip is even on the bar. Your torse should be positioned right in the middle of the bar and the distance between your torse and your right hand (which should be at the front) should be the same as the distance between your torse and your left hand (which should be to votre dos).
5. Now stand straight up with the poids. Conseil : vos pieds should be épaule width apart and your toes slightly pointed out.
6. Squat down by bending at the genous and keeping votre dos straight until your upper cuisses are parallel with le sol. Conseil : Keep votre dos as vertical as possible with le sol and votre tête up. Also remember to not let your genous go past your toes. Inspirez during this portion of le mouvement.
7. Now drive yourself back up to the position de départ by pushing with the feet . Conseil : Keep the bar hanging at arm''s length and your coudes locked with a slight bend. The arms only serve as hooks. Avoid doing any lifting with them. Do the lifting with your cuisses; not vos bras.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Jefferson_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Jerk Balance', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. This drill helps you learn to drive yourself low enough during the jerk and corrects those who move backward during le mouvement. Begin with the bar racked in the jerk position, with the épaules forward, torse upright, and the feet split slightly apart.
2. Initiate le mouvement as you would a normal jerk, dipping at the genous while keeping your torse vertical, and driving back up forcefully, using momentum and not vos bras to elevate the poids.
3. Keep the rear foot in place, using it to drive votre corps forward into a full split as you jerk the poids. Recover by standing up with the poids overhead.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Jerk_Balance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Jerk Dip Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. This movement strengthens the dip portion of the jerk. Begin with the bar racked in the jerk position, with the épaules forward to create a shelf and the bar lightly contacting the throat. The feet should be directly under the hanches, with the feet turned out as is comfortable.
2. Keeping the torse vertical, dip by flexing the genous, allowing them to travel forward and without moving the hanches to the rear. The dip should not be excessive. Return the poids to the position de départ by driving forcefully though the feet.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Jerk_Dip_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Jogging, Treadmill', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the treadmill and select the desired option from the menu. Most treadmills have a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Elevation can be adjusted to change the intensity of the workout.
2. Treadmills offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than jogging outside. A 150 lb person will burn almost 250 calories jogging for 30 minutes, compared to more than 450 calories running. Maintain proper posture as you jog, and only hold onto the handles when necessary, such as when dismounting or checking your heart rate.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Jogging_Treadmill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Keg Load', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. To load kegs, place the desired number a distance from the loading platform, typically 30-50 feet.
2. Begin by grabbing the close handle of the first keg, tilting it onto its side to grab the opposite edge of the bottom of the keg. Lift the keg up to your poitrine.
3. The higher you can place the keg, the faster you should be able to move to the platform. Shouldering is usually not allowed. Be sure to keep a firm hold on the keg. Move as quickly as possible to the platform, and load it, extending through your hanches, genous, and chevilles to get it as high as possible.
4. Revenez en position de départ to retrieve the next keg, and Répétez until the event is completed.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Biceps, Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Keg_Load/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
